/Pg 63 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
1326 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2184 0 R
/ActualText (Continuous Integration \(CI\): Developers frequently integrate their code changes into a shared repository, triggering automated builds and tests to catch issues early.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
1327 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2185 0 R
/ActualText (Continuous Delivery \(CD\): Code changes that pass CI are automatically deployed to staging or production environments, enabling faster and more frequent releases.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
1328 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2186 0 R
/ActualText (Infrastructure as Code \(IaC\): We've already discussed IaC in Chapter 5. It's a cornerstone of DevOps, allowing you to manage your infrastructure in a version-controlled and automated way.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
1329 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 2187 0 R
/ActualText (Monitoring and Logging: Continuously monitor your applications and infrastructure to identify and address issues proactively. Use centralized logging to gain insights into system behavior and performance.)
/Pg 63 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
